  "term": "auditory brainstem response",
  "definition": "Auditory brainstem response is an objective test that evaluates how the auditory nerve and brainstem pathways respond to sound. It is used to help identify possible neurological problems involving the eighth cranial nerve and connected hearing pathways up to the midbrain.",
